# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target
smoke-artifacts

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local config (may hold secrets); the example is tracked
axon.toml
!axon.toml.example

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local tooling state (worktrees, local settings) — never tracked
.claude/

# Node / web client
clients/web/node_modules/
clients/web/dist/
# Vite's dependency cache. It lands at the repo root when the dev server is
# started with the root as its working directory — which is how the web client
# gets pointed at a demo stack (smoke/tui/README.md), so this is easy to hit.
.vite/

# sqlx offline query cache (checked in only when intentional)
.sqlx/

# matrix-rust-sdk per-account state + crypto stores (runtime data, never tracked)
axon-data/

# Smoke harness failure artifacts (PTY transcripts, screens, logs, journals)
smoke-artifacts/

# Demo-corpus photographs (smoke/local-stack/corpus/media/photos). Only
# generated PLACEHOLDER stand-ins exist today — generate-placeholder-photos.mjs
# writes them here so the seeder can run end to end, and they must never reach a
# published recording. Delete this rule in the PR that lands the real, licensed
# photographs; see corpus/media/README.md.
smoke/local-stack/corpus/media/photos/
